I'd like to spice up NetHack-De a little bit, but without actually
changing the game play in a drastic way. That means, no SporkHack-De
or Slash'Em-De (for the time being :).

Essentially just fixing the most glaring bugs or shortcomings of
NetHack 3.4.3.

For example I don't consider fixing pudding farming part of this task
but I think fixing the polyself bug is part of it.

I already fixed the Astral Call bug - I hope in a subtle nethackish
way, not like GruntHack did - and randomized the Sokoban prize so one
has at least to use a !oOD or a charge of a crystal ball to determine
if the last sokoban level is worth the trouble.


For the "boring Gehennom" situation, the Heck� patch looks to me like
the way to go. And paxeds collection of new levels adds more diversity
to the levels before Gehennom.


But I haven't found any different level designs for good old Fort
Ludios. Since its introduction in NetHack 3.1.0 it has hardly been
changed.

So I tried and came up with two new levels. I'll post them as
followups to this post and if you have some comments about them I'd be
delighted to hear them.

Bye
